  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Little change to the forecast reasoning and\nsynoptic setups through the period. Where guidance is fairly \nwell clustered is with an amplified upper trough that will be \nshifting east out of the Central U.S. While there is still some \npotential for a cutoff low to develop, most guidance have now \ntrended towards more of a progressive and open wave as it moves \nthrough the Eastern U.S. Before that happens, low level flow \nwill be from a moist easterly direction over the next several\ndays, which will advect favorable regime for on and off light \nrain, esp for the coastal areas through Thursday. For the rest \nof today, light showers with eastward progressing shortwave \nenergy is not handled well by model guidance. Have inc pops \nmanually to account for isolated to widely scattered showers. \nThe same holds true through mid week, and ENC will cont under \ninfluence of e to se flow and hence a daily chance for widely \nsct showers. Have inc pops both Wed and Thu as a result. Don't \nexpect much in the way of accums, but enough to wet the ground \nin places, esp the further east in ENC.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Most guidance is now centering on the best \nchance of showers and even a few thunderstorms moving in Friday.\nPerhaps some WAA showers on Thu with warm front migrating\nthrough, as well as perhaps a rumble of thunder as well, but \nmain forcing mechanism for showers and storms arrives on Friday \nahead of a cold front. For this reason, pops are raised to\n40-50%. Of note, some guidance are showing anomalous moisture \nand higher- than- normal instability for early November, as \nindicated by EFI highlighting CAPE vals nearing the 80th \npercentile. This would support the potential of some higher \nrainfall rates and totals should this materialize. A few \nstronger storms may even materialize if timing of showers \narrives in the afternoon coinciding with peak heating. The other\naspect of the forecast that appears to be coming more clear \nthis week is the potential for above to well above normal \ntemperatures, especially Wednesday and Thursday, and esp during \nthe overnight periods. While record highs may not be broken, \nwarming low- level thicknesses in advance of the approaching \ntrough should support highs warming into the 70s, with some low \n80s possible inland. Meanwhile, overnight lows are forecast to \nbe closer to our normal highs for this time of year. Some record\nwarm lows may be in jeopardy. For reference, normal highs are \n65-70 for early November, with normal lows in the 40s inland and\n50s along the coast.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...Better agreement amongst 02/12Z model guidance\nwith fropa now late Friday, which will usher in a more\nseasonably dry airmass for the coming weekend. Return to mo\nsunny skies and highs in the 60s and lows generally in the 40s.",
